<main id="main">
  <section class="hero ink">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>What affects a deal</h1>
      <p class="lead">Buyers weigh several things before they consider company data. These are the considerations we review on a call. We do not publish prices, because every deal depends on the data and the terms.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-doccheck"/></svg></span>
        <h2>Rights to license</h2>
          <p>Can your company license this data? Contracts, customer terms and third-party content all matter.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-lock"/></svg></span>
        <h2>Consent and personal data</h2>
          <p>Removing names does not make data anonymous. Personal information needs its own review.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-clock"/></svg></span>
        <h2>Recency and history</h2>
          <p>Records that show how work changed over several years are usually more useful than a snapshot.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-grid"/></svg></span>
        <h2>Volume and variety</h2>
          <p>Buyers look at how much data there is and how many kinds of work it covers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-layers"/></svg></span>
        <h2>Structure and context</h2>
          <p>Decisions, outcomes and revisions are easier to use than raw files with no context.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card reveal">
        <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="icons.svg#i-doc"/></svg></span>
        <h2>Terms and exclusivity</h2>
          <p>Scope, length of license and payment timing shape the value of an offer, as well as the headline number.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">How each factor shapes a deal</h2>
      <p class="reveal">The same six factors, and what they change in practice. No figures, because the answer depends on the data and the terms.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap reveal">
        <table class="table">
          <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>What buyers look at</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Rights</td><td>Contracts, customer terms and third-party content</td><td>Decides whether the data can be licensed at all.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Personal data</td><td>Who appears in the records and in what detail</td><td>Removing names is not anonymization; it needs its own review.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>History</td><td>How far back the records go</td><td>Revisions and corrections are more useful than a snapshot.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Volume and variety</td><td>How much there is and how many kinds of work</td><td>A narrow but coherent dataset can beat a large, messy one.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Context</td><td>Whether decisions, outcomes and reasons are recorded</td><td>Records without context take longer to make usable.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Terms</td><td>Scope, length of license and payment timing</td><td>These shape the value of an offer, not just the headline number.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

